<p>By definition, if you are including the Triple Moon Consortium, you are acknowledging that they exist outside of one central human reality (as each of the moons are one such reality) &#8230; But I digress.</p>
<p>I think, even if you are avoiding making deep OCs, that you need to write these individual characters from a grounded perspective for the reader to relate to&#8230; otherwise, the events of this &quot;plot focused&quot; narrative will read fairly wooden. <strong>Especially</strong> if its not brief.</p>
<p>But that is my only concern, I am fairly interested in what you have to say. I would suggest reaching out to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daveyoufool" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2034230); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2034230&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607910944" alt="daveyoufool" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2034230)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daveyoufool" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2034230); return false;">daveyoufool</a></span> and getting his input on the usage of the Three Moons.</p>
<p>That being said, <strong><span style="color: green">GREENLIGHT</span></strong></p>

