<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional)</strong>: Mystery, Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: A seemingly innocent plate of Christmas gelatin (Festive season!), through further analysis, has been determined to be a cognitohazard employed by a gelatinous anomaly. It is able to detect prey by secreting pheromones into the air that when inhaled, awakens a predatory instinct within the gelatinous mass to envelop and consume affected prey item within a 5-meter radius of the plate.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: Field Agents dispatched to investigate an unexplained suburban disappearance of an entire family fails to report to Command. Ergo, an MTF team is deployed to follow up the disappearance, discovering human remains contained inside a mass of layered Christmas jello of an unknown origin. The object is retrieved and returned to an SCP Site wherein it is contained and the Foundation proceeds to conduct testing on the anomaly and gain additional understanding of its anomalous properties for optimal containment procedures.</p>
<p>After the SCP is confirmed a cognitohazard, it is suspected that the SCP was manufactured by a hitherto unknown Group of Interest. The Foundation launches a wider investigation into the origin of the SCP, sending Field Agents to return to the abandoned suburban home where it was originally discovered. The exploration log indicates that the agent discovers the original packaging and after finding out the brand name, another subsequent investigation reveals the identity of the Group of Interest that managed to evade Foundation radar up to this incident. The story ends with a footnote that ongoing surveillance and monitoring of the G.O.I is underway in order to assess the threat level of the parent G.O.I and ultimately deem whether Foundation intervention is necessary.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>: The hook starts with the mysterious disappearance of Foundation Field Agents in a peaceful suburban area with no record of kidnapping, homicides or break and entry crimes. This leads to the discovery of the SCP (Through an exploration log). Then the SCP Foundation attempts to understand the SCP's unknown properties (Experimentation log), allowing effective containment to be achieved. The SCP Foundation reasons from its nature as a cognitohazard that there was a strong possibility that the SCP was artificially engineered. The audience is constantly kept engaged by a linear narrative starting off with mystery that later unfolds into a deeper investigation of the SCP's origins.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: Have yet to determine a name for the G.O.I responsible for the manufacturing of the SCP, and have not yet decided whether the G.O.I are a belligerent or benevolent organisation.</p>

