						<a href="/forum/t-13909064/my-scp-idea">My SCP idea</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844151">
									

<p>It's a pretty simple concept. There's nothing wrong simplicity per se, but the simpler your idea, the more the article will need to be carried by the quality of the execution. The success of an article like this will depend pretty much entirely on your ability to create an atmosphere that draws the reader in and creates a sense of dread.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> High danger level and unic containiment procedures recommending you to poison yourself to avoid the anomaly</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In fiction, something being &quot;dangerous&quot; does not necessarily make it scary or interesting to the reader. Honestly, my attention isn't being grabbed by this, and the way you relied so strongly on a movie scene to convey your idea doesn't inspire my confidence in your ability execute this concept at the level of skill it requires. I understand that the language barrier might be an issue, though, so I won't hold it against you.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>we read a letter by the apartment past owner that tells us it’s backstory&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds pretty significant to the story, so it's strange that you've mentioned it as an afterthought here. What does the backstory tell us about the anomaly? How does it enhance the mood you want to convey? You're seeking a greenlight, but I can't evaluate your ideas properly if you haven't thought them through yet.</p>
<p>Overall it sounds like you have a pretty long article in mind, supported by some very broad ideas. That's doesn't mean you're doomed to fail by default, but it does present some rather sizeable challenges for you. If you decide to proceed, my advice for your next step is that you create a (reasonably) detailed outline for how you intend the article to flow from start to finish.</p>

							</div>

								
					
