<p>I like the idea of there being a mysterious star exerting influence over humans, and then gradually learning that the star is intelligent and acting deliberately to some terrible end. On the other hand, the &quot;Algernoning&quot; effect you described doesn't really interest me at all. I think part of the reason is that the Algernonification is tied to the victims' respective professions in such a straightforward way. There's no intrigue when the outcome of an experiment is so predictable, and there's no impact in inflicting misery on a series of characters without having some degree of emotional buildup and payoff.</p>
