<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5359</tt> (The Critter) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pickled29" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7116403); return false;">Pickled29</a></span> summarily deleted at -16 for being incomplete work on the mainsite. <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yossipossi" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2199269); return false;">Yossipossi</a></span> witnessed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5359</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong></p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5167</tt> (A Norse Gate) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/o-welles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6964254); return false;">O Welles</a></span> deleted at -13 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5167 is the designation given to both an anomalous site (SCP-5167-1) and the entity that affects it (SCP-5167-2). SCP-5167-1 is a laboratory built within an fortress dated to the early 1700's near the town of ███████ in the Black Forest, Germany.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5133</tt> (Sir Ruttlesurg) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cole-13" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6984611); return false;">Cole 13</a></span> deleted at -12 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Sir Ruttlesurg of England,</em><br />
<em>His teeth were sharp and his skin was quite bland,</em><br />
<em>he was so pale you'd think him undead,</em><br />
<em>If you do not sing him in song,</em></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5127</tt> (Ghost 'n sword) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/velja-vraccarevicc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6524034); return false;">Velja Vraccarevicc</a></span> deleted at -14 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5127 appears to be a large sword composed of an unknown metal. It was discovered in Serbia, Belgrade in 2007 after a massive amount of reports of ghostly figure slaughtering people.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5297</tt> (AN EDEN AT SIGHT) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/chazeasus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6915870); return false;">CHAZEASUS</a></span> deleted at -15 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-(redacted)-Prime is a subterranean cavity of a Holocene ecosystem with a land area of</p>
</blockquote>
<p>59.1&#160;km² located 1 kilometer under,50 kilometers west of Oral Kazakhstan, dated from about 17,000&#160;B.C.E. on carbon dating, its main biome is a Temperate Broadleaf Mixed Forest.</p>
<p>Feedback ported:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;from&nbsp;General&nbsp;Goose</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Question: What is the SCP here? There are so many entities linked to it, that it made me confused.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;from&nbsp;Cerastes&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If you and your co authors were working on it for seven months, you definitely should've tried to get criticism at some point. There's a lot of basic errors that could've been prevented by even a cursory review.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p><tt>scp-5587</tt> (The Breathability of Argon) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/solius" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5319086); return false;">solius</a></span> deleted at -13 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5587 is a gateway to an alternate dimension (SCP-5587-A) set into the trunk of an oak tree located on Mount Eisenhower at elevation of 4203 ft in White Mountain National Park, New Hampshire. When an organism comes in contact with SCP-5587, it is pulled through the tree into SCP-5587-A.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Feedback ported:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;from&nbsp;FinlandSite_Helsinki</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This SCP reminds me of the classic first SCPs of the site, more of an informational page than a thrilling story that most SCPs today must have to succeed. I think this is honestly by the book, it has all the detail we need, it’s not necessarily confusing, and it has almost zero grammatical or spelling errors which means the author put some work into making sure this is perfect. While I didn’t find this SCP particularly exciting it’s what the site was built on and feels more like an actual research log than a story that seems more like a tale which is what most current SCPs are like nowadays. Good work though! +1</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p><tt>wh-re-is-mine-own-gift</tt> (no title) by <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/joctaboom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6826831); return false;">Joctaboom</a></span> deleted at -14 and three votes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5129 is a female creature that has two forms the first being a female albino deer and the second being a black wolf. SCP-5129 is sapient and is capable of speech however, it speaks in Early Modern English. Whenever a human is seen by SCP-5129 the first thing it will do is ask for a gift by saying “Wh're is mine own gift.”</p>
</blockquote>
